60472eebe78b" 13194139534572 true] [17592186296263 1145 "Note that plugging in $x=1$ gives the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0}.$ However, we can use L'Hopital's rule to find this limit:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{5{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}-11}{4{x}^{3}-4} & ={lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{[5{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}-11]^{′}}{[4{x}^{3}-4]^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{15{x}^{2}+12x}{12{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{15(1)^{2}+12(1)}{12(1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{15+12}{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534572 true] [17592186296264 1000 #edb/ref 17592186296265 13194139534572 true] [17592186296264 1000 #edb/ref 17592186296266 13194139534572 true] [17592186296264 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534572 true] [17592186296264 1041 "field-1" 13194139534572 true] [17592186296264 1104 #edb/ref 17592186296266 13194139534572 true] [17592186296264 1110 #uuid "bdc83a8d-2600-5334-b8c5-80bdb79fd750" 13194139534572 true] [17592186296265 1034 "\\frac{4}{9}" 13194139534572 true] [17592186296265 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534572 true] [17592186296265 1111 #uuid "ebe3ac8d-a0cd-5920-8bb8-598a46e5d794" 13194139534572 true] [17592186296266 1034 "\\frac{9}{4}" 13194139534572 true] [17592186296266 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534572 true] [17592186296266 1111 #uuid "0e3eb583-b5b8-59df-a295-060954a5b36e" 13194139534572 true] [17592186296267 1017 #edb/ref 17592186296268 13194139534572 true] [17592186296267 1089 "q-336879" 13194139534572 true] [17592186296267 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534572 true] [17592186296267 1100 "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n$\\,{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{x}^{2}-4x}=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534572 true] [17592186296267 1113 #uuid "4a9c9c3f-7fbb-5a8d-b57d-d46d296a1a20" 13194139534572 true] [17592186296267 1145 "Note that plugging in $x=0$ gives the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0}.$ However, we can use L'Hopital's rule to find this limit:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{x}^{